vine 1.2.0
prefix: gameplay
title: Remaining Caravan demo gameplay
---
[root] Plan remaining demo gameplay from canonical design (planning)
Files: gameplay.vine; proposals/demo-gameplay.md; spec/**; proposals/**; crates/caravan-demo/**; evidence/**
Do: Turn the existing Caravan domain, temporal, branch, persistence, input, and rendering commitments into one ordered player-facing demo plan. Keep the game-facing meaning above host and transport plumbing, and keep implementation downstream of an explicit gameplay ruling.
Accept: The design inventory distinguishes existing substrate from player-facing gaps; one first demo loop is selected from the old design commitments; its commands, temporal controls, composition, and evidence have disjoint owners; the full demo remains an immutable-worldline toy; and no generic engine extraction is introduced without a concrete repeated boundary.
-> design-inventory
-> first-loop
-> interaction-surface
-> temporal-surface
-> demo-composition
-> demo-presentation
-> gameplay-evidence
-> boundary-polish
